essive to me  uh the track record on free speech as we  we have a report from cnbc about uh  musk's record on free speech it's not a  great record he has sought control over  what journalist bloggers analysts and  others say about his businesses he's  reportedly cancelled people's  a blogger's tesla order when the blogger  blogged something elon musk didn't like  so what does this mean for twitter i  have absolutely no idea it could be bad  there's no doubt about it but i think  the problem i'm having is that all of  the discussion 99 of the discussion is  based around people's pre-existing  opinion about elon musk as a uniquely  great figure or as a uniquely terrible  figure and that seems extraordinarily  short-sighted my main concern with musk  buying twitter  is that of consolidation and monopoly  i don't really love the idea  of one person controlling so many major  companies elon musk's going to control  twitter  and tesla which is now i believe by  market cap the largest auto manufacturer  in the united states  uh and spacex which is i believe the  most important private space exploration  come it start the consolidation of power  is my uh primary concern will trump be  back on twitter as a result like is elon  musk planning to unban trump i have  absolutely no idea trump says he doesn't  plan to go back on that may change that  seems like a minor detail at this point  so let me know your thoughts about the  twitter takeover but try to make them  substantive rather than driven by just  your opinion of elon musk as an  individual which the right just is  they're praying at the altar of musk  and it seems unhinged  and also i'm seeing some on the left who  are just  painting him as a uniquely evil  character which also doesn't strike me  as accurate let me know your thoughts  i'm on twitter at deepakman  one of our sponsors is called privacy  privacy is a totally free service that  i've been using for years privacy lets  me create virtual payment cards with one